  "simplified": [
    "A single cable descends outboard of the western carriageways and returns through a half-ellipse below both girder soffits. The eastern anchoring saddles sit outside the traffic surfaces.",
    "The adjacent box girders use a bevelled soffit. The approach to Oakland includes 600 m along the mapped skyway curve and four intermediate support stations.",
    "Four tapered tower shafts, enlarged linking beams, simplified suspenders and a single saddle housing replace the smaller steelwork. The bicycle path and road furniture are omitted.",
    "The western cutoff is the SAS approach 37.5 m behind W2. The eastern cutoff follows 600 m of the curved skyway from the SAS transition. Both pairs of deck ends meet grounded abutments."
